      "checkerUrl": null,
      "boundaryDescription": "...designated the Selective Licensing area of Wigston and South Wigston (\"The Designation\") as delineated in blue on the map at Annex A which includes, but is not limited to, an area bounded by Granville Road and Brighton Avenue to the north, Avondale Road to the east, Countesthorpe Road to the South and Saffron Road and Hindoostan Avenue to the west.",
      "evidence": "The 182 streets above are transcribed from Annex B (pages 5-6) of the sealed public notice 'Designation of an area for Selective Licensing, Section 80, Housing Act 2004', titled 'Wigston and South Wigston Designation of an Area for Selective Licensing 2025'. The PDF is a scanned image with no text layer (pdftotext returns only form feeds), so it was rendered with PyMuPDF and transcribed visually, then each table column was re-rendered separately at 330 dpi as an independent cross-check; both extractions agreed exactly. Annex B has three 'Street Name' columns: column 1 carries the sub-heading 'South Wigston' (first 64 entries here) and columns 2-3 form one continuous unlabelled alphabetical run for Wigston Magna (remaining 118). 'Cleveland Road (up to 44)' is the ONLY house-number restriction in the whole annex and is preserved verbatim. Two names are transcribed as printed rather than corrected: 'Healthfield Road' (the real street is Heathfield Road) and 'St Thomas' Road' with a right single quote. SCOPE CAVEAT: the council web page says the scheme 'only covers private-rented houses', but the notice itself says it 'applies to any privately-rented property, subject to any statutory exceptions' (mandatory-licensable HMOs, social housing, and the Selective Licensing of Houses (Specified Exemptions) (England) Order 2006). The predecessor South Wigston Ward scheme ran 5 May 2020 to 4 May 2025 and has lapsed; there was a roughly six-month gap. No postcode list and no licensing-area address checker are published; Annex A (page 4) is a blue-outlined OS map from which no street was inferred."
